            if (isOrderGroup(item)) return null;
            const meta = ORDER_STATUS_META[item.status];
            return <Label theme={meta.theme}>{meta.title}</Label>;
        },
        size: 160,
    },
    {id: 'date', header: 'Дата', accessorFn: ..., cell: format date, size: 170},
    {id: 'positions', header: 'Позиции', accessorFn..., size: 100},
    {id: 'amount', header: 'Сумма', accessorFn..., cell: formatAmount, size: 140},
    {id: 'address', header: 'Адрес доставки', accessorFn..., size: 280},
];
```

Default cell for columns without `cell`: TanStack renders getValue via flexRender default — default cell renderer renders `info.getValue()`. Fine.

getGroupTitle:

```tsx
const getGroupTitle = React.useCallback((row: Row<OrderTableItem>) => {
    const item = row.original;
    if (!isOrderGroup(item)) return '';
    const total = item.orders.reduce((sum, order) => sum + order.amount, 0);
    return `${ORDER_STATUS_META[item.status].groupTitle} · ${formatAmount(total)}`;
}, []);
```

getIsGroupHeaderRow: `(row) => row.getCanExpand()`.

Table render inside page:

```tsx
<div className="orders-page">
    <Flex alignItems="baseline" justifyContent="space-between" gap={4}>
        <Text variant="header-1">Заказы</Text>
        <Text variant="body-2" color="secondary">Выбрано: {selectedCount}</Text>
    </Flex>
    <Text variant="body-2" color="secondary">Строки сгруппированы по статусу заказа. Чтобы изменить порядок колонок, перетащите заголовок колонки. Чекбоксы слева выделяют строки.</Text>
    <div className="orders-page__table">
        <ColumnReorderingProvider table={table} onReorder={handleColumnReorder}>
            <Table table={table} getGroupTitle={getGroupTitle} getIsGroupHeaderRow={...} stickyHeader />
        </ColumnReorderingProvider>
    </div>
</div>
```

Column order state: `const [columnOrder, setColumnOrder] = React.useState<string[]>([])` and pass `state: {..., columnOrder}` + `onColumnOrderChange: setColumnOrder` (per docs when controlling). onReorder handler also setColumnOrder. Empty array = default order initially.

selectedCount:
```tsx
const selectedCount = table.getSelectedRowModel().rows.filter((row) => !row.getCanExpand()).length;
```
Hmm getSelectedRowModel includes group rows; groups get selected when all subRows selected (TanStack auto). Filter via isOrderGroup(row.original) instead. `!row.getCanExpand()` equivalent. Fine either way.

Table height: `.orders-page` is flex column height 100%; `.orders-page__table { flex: 1; min-height: 0; overflow: auto; border: 1px solid var(--g-color-line-generic); border-radius: var(--g-border-radius-l); }` and `stickyHeader` makes header stick within the scroll container. Does stickyHeader work inside overflow container? stickyHeader uses position: sticky on thead — works within nearest scrolling ancestor. Good.

renderContent: `<div style={{height: '100%'}}>`? The AsideHeader content container — I don't know its exact styling; it likely fills. I'll give .orders-page height: 100% and the parent chain: renderContent returns content rendered in `.gn-aside-header-content`? Let me not over-engineer: set `.orders-page {height: 100vh}`? Risky (top alert offset). Better: check AsideHeader content wrapper styling quickly — content container likely flexes. I'll use height: 100% and add fallback: if parent has no height, page still renders (table area scrolls internally only if height constrained). To be safe use `height: 100vh; box-sizing: border-box` on .orders-page? If AsideHeader content already handles full height, 100vh ≈ fine visually (no top alert). I'll check the AsideHeader.css for content class quickly... Actually the docs say "CSS-variable --gn-aside-header-size contains actual navigation size". Content is to the right. I'll just set `.orders-page {height: 100vh}` minus nothing — acceptable for eval, but overflow could double-scroll. Simpler and robust: page wrapper `padding`, and let the whole content area scroll naturally (no inner scroll, no stickyHeader). But stickyHeader is a nice touch... 

Decision: keep it simple and correct — table wrapper without fixed height, page scrolls as document within AsideHeader content region. stickyHeader requires a scroll container with bounded height; without it, sticky just won't trigger (harmless). I'll still pass stickyHeader + give the content wrapper height 100% chain: `.g-root` has height? No.

Let me check how AsideHeader lays out content — quick grep of its CSS: `.gn-aside-header__content`? Let me check quickly.

